codex
The PRC path has no lock or multiprocessing primitive. The scale-specific failure comes from its per-class execution pattern: for every training minibatch it runs two model forwards per shared class (up to 200 forwards for CIFAR-100), unlike reliability’s batched memory processing. I’m collapsing those identical per-class MSE computations into two batched forwards and removing the in-loss CUDA scalar synchronization.
apply patch
